{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Interactions.inductiveGBReduction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Interactions.inductiveGBReduction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.inductiveGBReduction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.inductiveGBReduction","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/inductiveGBReduction.lean#L41-L87","doc":"**Proposition statement** (from manuscript):\n\nLet $\\mathcal{N}_{\\leq k}$ denote the Gröbner--Shirshov normal form\nof the first $k$ nucleons in $H_k(q)$.  The inductive step*\n\n$$\n  \\mathcal{N}_{\\leq k+1}\n  =\n  r\\!\\bigl(\n    \\mathcal{N}_{\\leq k}\n    \\cdot C(\\mathfrak{N}_k, \\mathfrak{N}_{k+1}; \\sigma_g)\n    \\cdot \\mathfrak{N}_{k+1},\\;\n    G\n  \\bigr)\n$$\n\n*produces a normal form with at most $\\binom{A-1}{\\lfloor(A-1)/2\\rfloor}$\nterms, where $r(\\cdot, G)$ is the Gröbner--Shirshov division\nalgorithm\n([nuclear Gröbner reduction](#prop:nuclear-groebner-reduction)).*\n\n*The total computation for $\\mathcal{N}(Z, N)$ requires\n$O(A^2)$ multiplications and $O(A^3)$ Hecke reduction steps.*\n\n## Proof\n\nAt each inductive step, the product\n$\\mathcal{N}_{\\leq k} \\cdot C \\cdot \\mathfrak{N}_{k+1}$ has\nat most $|\\mathcal{N}_{\\leq k}| \\times 2 \\times 6$ terms\n(the crossing $C$ has at most 2 terms, and the nucleon NF has\n6 terms).  The Gröbner--Shirshov reduction eliminates all\n$\\sigma_i^2$ via the Hecke relation and sorts via Yang--Baxter,\nproducing a normal form of bounded size.\n\nThe key identity enabling this is the nuclear Gröbner reduction.\n\nWe **name** the resulting bound (pattern C of the vacuity-fix\nplaybook) as a `Prop` over the context's primitive step-count data,\nrather than projecting it from self-assuming `h_*` fields: the\nnormal form has at most $\\binom{A-1}{\\lfloor(A-1)/2\\rfloor}$ terms,\nwith $O(A^2)$ multiplications and $O(A^3)$ Hecke reduction steps.\nAn instance of this proposition is the open complexity claim. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:inductive-gb-reduction","label":"prop:inductive-gb-reduction","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/inductive-gb-reduction.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.InductiveGBReductionContext.n_reduction_steps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.InductiveGBReductionContext.n_reduction_steps","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/inductiveGBReduction.lean#L39-L39","doc":"Number of Hecke reduction steps performed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.InductiveGBReductionContext.n_multiplications","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.InductiveGBReductionContext.n_multiplications","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/inductiveGBReduction.lean#L37-L37","doc":"Number of multiplications performed by the full inductive\nreduction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.InductiveGBReductionContext.NF_size","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.InductiveGBReductionContext.NF_size","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/inductiveGBReduction.lean#L34-L34","doc":"NF size at strand count `k` (cumulative inductive reduction). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.InductiveGBReductionContext.A_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.InductiveGBReductionContext.A_eq","kind":"theorem","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/inductiveGBReduction.lean#L32-L32","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.InductiveGBReductionContext.A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.InductiveGBReductionContext.A","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/inductiveGBReduction.lean#L31-L31","doc":"Mass number `A = Z + N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.InductiveGBReductionContext.N","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.InductiveGBReductionContext.N","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/inductiveGBReduction.lean#L29-L29","doc":"Neutron number `N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.InductiveGBReductionContext.Z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.InductiveGBReductionContext.Z","kind":"def","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/inductiveGBReduction.lean#L27-L27","doc":"Proton number `Z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.InductiveGBReductionContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.InductiveGBReductionContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/inductiveGBReduction.lean#L25-L25","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.InductiveGBReductionContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.InductiveGBReductionContext","kind":"class","line":18,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/inductiveGBReduction.lean#L18-L39","doc":"Carrier for the `inductiveGBReduction` data — only the\nprimitive, non-conclusory fields (pattern C): mass number,\ncumulative normal-form size, and the multiplication / reduction\nstep counts.  The three bounds (the manuscript's `≤ binom`,\n`≤ A²`, `≤ A³`) are **not** fields here — they are the named\nproposition `inductiveGBReduction` below, so the claim is\nstated, not self-assumed. ","signatureChunk":0}]}